Mesh app for the ESP-NOW mesh (needs espnow-mesh.patch)

Adds apps/mesh.py, a "Mesh" app that shows how many nodes the badge hears and
the latest text messages, and blinks the last LED for every new packet. The
badge picks up any app in apps/ by itself, so nothing else changes. Without
the mesh installed, the app says so instead of breaking anything. Paths are
relative to the badge's root folder, the one holding main.py.

Made against Hack-a-Day/2026-Billboard_Badge at 5945518 (2026-11-08), where
the badge's root folder is firmware/badge. It only adds files, so it applies
to any version of the firmware.

Apply from the folder holding main.py:
    git apply mesh-app.patch
    (or: patch -p1 < mesh-app.patch)
Apply from a clone of github.com/Hack-a-Day/2026-Billboard_Badge:
    git apply --directory=firmware/badge mesh-app.patch
Apply from the supercon10 project root:
    git apply --directory=device patches/mesh-app.patch
Then copy apps/mesh.py to the badge.

Files:
    apps/mesh.py         new file, 200 lines

